   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "DRUG RASH",
   "bbox": [
    371.8,
    48.7,
    470.1,
    71.0
   ],
   "key": "p88-d05141f4"
  },
  {
   "id": "p88-out-e02",
   "page": 88,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "• A drug rash can be caused by any medication: antibiotics, antiseizure medication, ART (efavirenz, abacavir), TB medication, co-trimoxazole, TB preventive treatment (TPT), allopurinol, NSAIDs (like ibuprofen). • Suspect a drug rash in a patient with a generalised rash which appeared within 3 months of starting a new medication.",
   "bbox": [
    51.0,
    89.7,
    506.9,
    119.9
   ],
   "key": "p88-42170e13"
  },
  {
   "id": "p88-out-e03",
   "page": 88,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "1If SBP < 80, pulse ≥ 100, respiratory rate > 30, confusion/restlessness, weakness, shock likely. 2Markers of severity: face/tongue swelling, difficulty breathing, BP < 90/60, temperature ≥ 38°C, abdominal pain, vomiting/diarrhoea, involves mouth/eyes/genitals, blisters/ peeling/raw areas, jaundice, unwell/malaise/fatigue/body pain.",
   "bbox": [
    34.0,
    535.0,
    802.6,
    552.0
   ],
   "key": "p88-1d382f6c"
  },
  {
   "id": "p88-out-e04",
   "page": 88,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Approach to the patient with a drug rash not needing urgent attention",
   "bbox": [
    281.3,
    265.0,
    560.7,
    276.0
   ],
   "key": "p88-e91e278e"
  },
  {
   "id": "p88-out-e05",
   "page": 88,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Is patient on ART, TB medication, co-trimoxazole or TPT?",
   "bbox": [
    318.8,
    275.8,
    523.2,
    286.0
   ],
   "key": "p88-20b9380c"
  },
  {
   "id": "p88-out-e06",
   "page": 88,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Refer to doctor/discuss with MIC hotline 200 whether to continue, change or stop medication: • If on ART: - Continue unless on abacavir, and abacavir hypersensitivity reaction (AHR) likely 131. - If on nevirapine or efavirenz, doctor to switch ART 132. • If itch, give chlorphenamine 4mg at night, or 8 hourly for up to 5 days. • Check ALT and eosinophil count. • Advise to return urgently if rash worsens or markers of severity1 occur.",
   "bbox": [
    119.1,
    326.3,
    504.0,
    397.1
   ],
   "key": "p88-ee41c9c5"
  },
  {
